From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:25:26 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] formula: build and recognise shifted copies without
 rebuilding the tree

Adds three primitives next to `shift_relative`, each defined to agree with it exactly:

- `shifted(e, dr, dc)`: `shift_relative(e.clone(), dr, dc)` in one pass over a borrowed tree (the
  clone-then-map path allocates every node twice);
- `is_shifted_copy(base, dr, dc, other)`: whether `other` is `base` copied (dr, dc) away, i.e.
  the two cells hold the same formula in R1C1 terms, compared without building the copy;
- `shift_stays_on_sheet(e, dr, dc)`: whether that copy keeps every reference on the sheet.

They are what a shared formula representation needs: build a cell's tree on demand, find runs
of copies, and tell when two moves compose into one.
